vernment buildings in the  area following news the influential  cleric was quitting after a political  deadlock prevented him from forming a  new government while ordering his  followers to stand down al-sadr also  apologized for the violence which left  more than 400 others hurt  where are canada's family doctors ahead  the systemic strain driving away these  medical professionals  a crisis continues to unfold in  emergency rooms across canada staffing  shortages unprecedented wait times and  full-out closures are being seen from  coast to coast to coast as part of our  series code blue global news recently  spent the day inside one emergency  department and found the er capacity  crunch is a symptom of a much larger  problem jeff semple explains  across the country hospital emergency  rooms are on life support  this toronto er is seeing more patients  arriving with advanced illness and they  often have something else in common  there is quite a  large number of patients who doesn't  have a family doctor how are you i'm  good thanks how are you millions of  canadians do not have access to a family  physician including the mcneils it's  been a challenge  their daughter was suffering stomach  pains the family spent hours in a  hospital emergency room for what turned  out to be a flu  it was the sort of thing we normally  wouldn't have taken a child to emergency  for it was appropriate for a family  doctor but we didn't have the chance  when they first moved to pei in 2018 the  wait list for a family doctor was four  years  but they were just told it will likely  be another four years  there's a lot of pressures on family  medicine right now the head of the  college of family physicians says the  problem is getting worse  family physicians  either  reducing their hours  going into other focused practices or  most concerning for me  medical students coming out and choosing  specialties other other than family  medicine the number of medical school  graduates choosing a career in family  medicine has been dropping for a decade  good morning one how are you  part of the reason for that reluctance  family doctors are required to run their  own business with a lot of overhead and  little support if you're trying to  navigate all of this complexity by  yourself without administrative support  without infrastructure without  additional team members it's not going  to work to that end dr ali damji adopted  a different model his office includes  nurses dietitians physiotherapists  social workers and admin staff the  so-called family health team model can  be found across the country but in small  numbers  dr damji believes it should play a  larger role to attract more medical  professionals to family medicine if  patients have access to comprehensive  primary care we see better health  outcomes better satisfaction lower  health care costs to the system  because patients without a family doctor  are much more likely to end up here  jeff semple global news toronto  the world health organization says it is  still possible to eliminate the monkey  pox outbreak in europe the who says case  counts are slowing in several european  countries including france germany and  portugal but to eliminate the disease  there needs to be an urgent boost in the  limited supply of vaccine  drinking danger next the new data on  just how much alcohol is too much for  your health  many people enjoy the odd cold beer on a  hot summer day but those drinks could be  more dangerous than you even think a new  report says alcohol is not good for your  health even in small amounts this is  according to the canadian center on  substance use and addiction drinking can  increase your risk of cancer heart  disease and stroke it also suggests  mandatory labeling of alcoholic  beverages to reflect safe portion sizes  but as karen lieberman explains it's  unclear if this will be enough for  people to rethink the way they drink  when it comes to alcohol consumption and  the question how much is too much the  message may be changing to me i know  that alcohol is uh usually like bad for  you but i didn't know like how bad it  was even in small quantities drinking  alcohol can have a big impact points out  the canadian center on substance use and  addiction with this new report we viewed  alcohol  consumption as harmful only if you have  dependents but we know that alcohol  consumption even  in the low amounts causes harm to the  entire body the ccsa's report found  having two drinks or fewer per week puts  an individual at low risk three to six  drinks per week poses a moderate risk  for developing certain cancers but  health risks become increasingly high  when someone has seven drinks or more  per week unlike almost any other risk  factor alcohol consumption affects the  whole body so we're talking about things  like infectious diseases but then we  also have neurological diseases so  alcohol impacts the brain we also have  cardiovascular diseases it affects the  heart there is also a strong link  between moderate to heavy drinking and  cancer this includes female breast as  well as head and neck so those kind of  your mouth your throat your larynx and  your esophageal as well as colorectal  and liver cancers doctors are calling  for mandatory alcohol warning labeling  like has long been the case with tobacco  and cannabis there is a huge lack of  understanding that a tall can of beer is  not one standard drink that sits one and  a half that a bottle of wine is actually  five standard drinks in canada a  standard drink has  13.45 grams of alcohol regardless of the  kind of drink you're having that kind of  thing does run in my family you know the  abuse of alcohol so  i think it's good that people are  talking about it more often and i  believe that giving people information  about what they're consuming  helps them to make more informed choices  so the next time you raise a glass it  might be something else karen lieberman  global news toronto  and that's global national for this  tuesday night i'm farah nasser on behalf  of our whole crew here i wanted to thank  you so much for spending part of your  evening with us  tonight's your canada is rayboro ontario  we love seeing your canada so please  email us those photos to viewers at  globalnational.com  until tomorrow take care of yourselves  and each other good night  [Music]  you
 

